extends layoutPortfolio

block content

  section.hero
    .wrap
      p.hero-kicker ~/Dovydas
      h1 Dovydas Griškevičius
      p.hero-role Full-stack developer, building small useful things
      p.hero-lede.
        I design and build web applications end to end — from database schema
        to the page you're looking at. Most of what's below started as a
        problem I wanted solved for myself.
      .hero-actions
        a.btn.btn-outline(href="#projects") View projects
        a.btn.btn-primary(href="/contact#hire") Hire me

  section#projects
    .wrap
      .section-head
        h2 Selected projects
        a(href="/contact") Have a project in mind? Let's talk →

      .projects-list
        if projects && projects.length
          each project in projects
            a.project-row(href=`/projects/project/${project.id}`)
              .project-thumb
                img(src=project.cover_image || '/img/placeholder.jpg', alt="")
              .project-info
                h3= project.name
                p= project.description
                if project.tags && project.tags.length
                  .project-tags
                    each tag in project.tags
                      span= tag
              .project-links
                if project.url
                  a(href=project.url, target="_blank", rel="noopener") Live demo
                if project.github_url
                  a(href=project.github_url, target="_blank", rel="noopener") GitHub
        else
          p No projects yet

  section
    .wrap
      .about-grid
        .about-photo
        .about-copy
          p.eyebrow-free-heading(style="margin-bottom:20px;") A bit about how I work
          p.
            I'm mostly self-taught, which means I've broken most things at
            least once before learning why they broke. I like backend and
            database work in particular — figuring out the right shape for
            data tends to make everything built on top of it easier.
          p.
            Outside of code I'm usually reading, hiking, or slowly
            rebuilding this site for the third time.
          a.btn.btn-outline(href="/about", style="margin-top:12px;") More about me
